# Own-wording Tome of Heroes spells, chunk C (Feint to Hunter's Endurance). TEXT = {name: text}.
TEXT = {
"Feint": "As you make an attack against a creature, a flickering duplicate of you appears for a moment. You have Advantage on the next attack roll you make against that target before the end of your next turn, as it is distracted by your illusory copy.",
"Fey Food": "You enchant up to 1 pound of food or 1 gallon of drink within range with fey magic and choose one effect. For the duration, a creature that consumes it, up to four creatures per pound or gallon, makes a Charisma saving throw or suffers the effect. Sleep: the creature falls Unconscious for 1 hour, ending if it takes damage or someone uses an action to wake it. Charm: the creature is Charmed by you for 1 hour. If you or your allies do anything harmful to it, it repeats the save, ending the spell on a success. Forgetfulness: the creature remembers only fragments of the past hour. Remove curse or greater restoration restores its memory.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** You can enchant 1 more pound of food or gallon of drink for each slot level above 3rd.",
"Fey-Touched Blade": "You touch a nonmagical weapon and fill it with fey magic. Pick Force, Psychic, Necrotic or Radiant. Until the spell ends the weapon is magical and deals an extra 1d4 damage of that type to any target it hits.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** You can imbue one more weapon for each slot level above 2nd.",
"Forced Reposition": "One creature you can see within range is teleported to a free space you can see up to 60 feet above you. The space can be open air, a balcony, a ledge or any other surface above you. An unwilling creature that succeeds on a Constitution saving throw is unaffected. A creature teleported into open air falls at once, taking fall damage as normal, unless it can fly or otherwise stop a fall. A creature cannot be teleported into a solid object.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** You can target one more creature for each slot level above 4th, all within 30 feet of each other. They need not go to the same place.",
"Frenzied Bolt": "You send a bolt of rainbow colors at a creature within range. Make a ranged spell attack. On a hit the target takes 3d8 damage of a type found by rolling a d10: 1 Acid, 2 Cold, 3 Fire, 4 Force, 5 Lightning, 6 Necrotic, 7 Poison, 8 Psychic, 9 Radiant, 10 Thunder. If your attack roll before modifiers was odd, the bolt leaps to a new target of your choice within range that this casting has not yet targeted, needing a new attack roll. It keeps leaping until you roll an even number, miss, or run out of targets. You and your allies are valid targets if you are lucky or unlucky.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** You create one more bolt for each slot level above 2nd. Each target can be hit once per casting, not once per bolt.",
"Furious Wail": "You scream in white-hot fury and pierce the minds of up to five creatures within range. Each target makes a Charisma saving throw. On a failure it takes 10d10 + 30 Psychic damage and is Stunned until the end of its next turn. On a success it takes half damage.",
"Fuse Armor": "Choose a manufactured metal object with movable parts that you can see within range, such as a drawbridge winch or a suit of medium or heavy metal armor. Its parts fuse for the duration. A pulley will not turn and armor joints will not bend. A creature wearing affected armor has its speed reduced by 10 feet and Disadvantage on weapon attacks and Strength or Dexterity ability checks. At the end of each of its turns, it makes a Strength saving throw, ending the spell on the armor on a success. A creature touching an affected object that is not armor can use its action for a Strength check against your spell save DC, ending the spell on the object on a success. A construct you target makes a Strength saving throw or has its speed reduced by 10 feet and Disadvantage on weapon attacks, repeating the save at the end of each of its turns and ending the spell on a success.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** You can target one more object for each slot level above 2nd, all within 30 feet of each other.",
"Gale": "You summon a storm to batter oncoming enemies. For the duration, freezing rain and wild wind fill a 20-foot-tall cylinder with a 300-foot radius centered on a point you choose within range. You must be outdoors to cast it, and the spell ends early if you move somewhere with no clear path to the sky. The area is heavily obscured and exposed flames are doused. The ground is slick difficult terrain, and a flying creature in the area must land by the end of its turn or fall. When a creature enters the area for the first time on a turn or starts its turn there, it makes a Constitution saving throw, taking 1d6 Cold damage on a failure. A creature concentrating inside the area must succeed on a Constitution saving throw against your spell save DC or lose Concentration.",
"Gird the Spirit": "Your magic shields a target creature from the life-draining energy of undead. For the duration it is immune to undead effects that reduce its ability scores, such as a shadow's Strength Drain, or its hit point maximum, such as a specter's Life Drain. It does not prevent the damage of those attacks, only the reduction.",
"Glare": "You cast a disdainful glare at up to two creatures you can see within range. Each makes a Wisdom saving throw or takes no actions on its next turn as it reassesses its life choices. If it fails by 5 or more, it takes no actions on its next two turns.",
"Glyph of Shifting": "You trace a hidden glyph on a surface or object you touch. When you cast the spell, you can also pick a destination you know, within 5 miles and on the same plane. A creature unaware of the glyph that touches it makes a Wisdom saving throw or is teleported to the destination. If you set none, it takes 4d4 Force damage and is knocked Prone. The glyph disappears when triggered or when the spell ends.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** The duration increases by 24 hours and the maximum distance to the destination by 5 miles for each slot level above 2nd.",
"Going in Circles": "You make natural terrain in a 1-mile cube hard to cross. A creature in the area has Disadvantage on Wisdom (Survival) checks to follow tracks or travel safely, as paths twist and turn nonsensically. Only perception changes, not the terrain. A creature that succeeds on two Survival checks inside sees through the illusion and sees the false twists laid over the land. A creature that leaves and re-enters before the spell ends is affected again, even if it succeeded earlier. A creature with truesight sees through it and is unaffected. A creature that casts find the path automatically finds its way out. When you cast the spell you can set a password. A creature that speaks it on entering the area sees the illusion and is unaffected. Casting it at the same spot every day for one year makes it last until dispelled.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** With a 4th-level slot you can concentrate for up to 8 hours. With a slot of 5th level or higher, up to 24 hours.",
"Harry": "You instill an overwhelming sense of insecurity and terror in a target within range. It makes a Wisdom saving throw. On a failure it has Disadvantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks to avoid your notice and is Frightened of you while you are in its line of sight. While you are within 1 mile of it, you have Advantage on Wisdom (Survival) checks to track it, and it cannot rest, terrified you are just around the corner. It repeats the save once every 10 minutes, ending the spell on a success. A target that succeeds on the first save is unaffected, and you cannot use this spell on it again for 24 hours.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** With a 6th-level slot, you can concentrate for up to 8 hours and the target repeats the save once each hour. With a slot of 8th level or higher, up to 24 hours and the target repeats the save every 8 hours.",
"Harrying Hounds": "When you cast the spell, choose a direction, such as north or southeast. Each creature in a 20-foot-radius sphere centered on a point you choose within range makes a Wisdom saving throw when you cast it, and is affected on a failure. An affected creature that travels moves at a fast pace in the opposite direction, believing a pack of dogs or wolves follows from the chosen direction. When it is not traveling, it is Frightened of your chosen direction. It occasionally hears howls or sees glowing eyes at the edge of its vision that way. It will not stop at a destination, instead pacing half-circles around it until the effect ends. It repeats the save at the end of each 4-hour period, ending the effect on itself on a success. It takes the safest route unless it has nowhere to go, such as a cliff edge. If it cannot safely move away, it cowers in place, defending itself but otherwise taking no actions, and repeats the save every minute, ending the effect on a success. The effect is suspended while the creature is in combat, so it can move as needed to face hostile creatures.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** The duration increases by 4 hours for each slot level above 5th. A creature that travels more than 8 hours risks Exhaustion as on a forced march.",
"Heart to Heart": "For the duration, you and a creature you touch stay stable and Unconscious if either of you drops to 0 hit points while the other has at least 1. If you touch a dying creature, it becomes stable but stays Unconscious at 0 hit points. If both of you are at 0 hit points, you both make death saving throws as normal. When either of you regains hit points, that person may split them between you both if you are within 60 feet of each other.",
"Heart-Seeking Arrow": "The next time you make a ranged weapon attack during the spell, the ammunition, or the weapon itself if thrown, seeks the target's vital organs. Make the attack roll as normal. On a hit it deals an extra 6d6 damage of the weapon's type. On a miss it still deals half as much, as it streaks unerringly toward the target. If the attack reduces the target to 0 hit points, the target has Disadvantage on its next death saving throw, and if it dies it can be restored only by true resurrection or wish. The spell has no effect on undead or constructs.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** The extra damage on a hit increases by 1d6 for each slot level above 4th.",
"High Ground": "With a word and a gesture you raise a 10-foot-tall hillock at a point you choose within range. You must be outdoors. The hillock is up to 30 feet long and 15 feet wide, in a line. A creature whose space it cuts through is pushed to one side or to the top, your choice. The ranged attack distance of a creature on top is doubled against targets at a lower elevation. The GM may grant creatures on top other effects of elevation, such as Advantage against those below, being easier to spot, or longer sight. The steep sides are difficult to climb. A creature at the bottom must succeed on a Strength (Athletics) or Dexterity (Acrobatics) check against your spell save DC to reach the top. The spell cannot manipulate stone construction, and rocks and structures shift aside. If the hillock would make a structure unstable, it fails to form in the structure's spaces. It does not directly affect plant growth, and plants rise with it.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** For each slot level above 3rd, you can add 5 feet to the width or 10 feet to the length.",
"Hunter's Endurance": "You call on the land to sustain you as you hunt. Name or describe a creature familiar to you. If you are not familiar with it, you need a fingernail, lock of hair, bit of fur or drop of blood from it as the material component. Until the spell ends you have Advantage on all Wisdom (Perception) and Wisdom (Survival) checks to find and track the target, and you must actively pursue it as if under a geas. You also do not suffer Exhaustion levels gained from pursuing it, such as from lack of rest or environmental hazards between you and the target. When the spell ends you suffer all Exhaustion levels it suspended. The spell ends after 24 hours, when the target is dead, when the target is on a different plane, or when the target is Restrained in your line of sight.",
}
